2026-09-24 12:23:07 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"be7fe2a4-925e-4d9e-84f7-b622b1f02f43","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-aws-object-storage-demo/be7fe2a4-925e-4d9e-84f7-b622b1f02f43.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/aws-object-storage-demo","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","agent_id":"a3a009a85bd1a9278","agent_type":"ue-ca:implementation:exceptions-developer","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/iss-ue-ca-plugin/claude/uac/ue-ca/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/exceptions.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/iss-ue-ca-plugin/claude/uac/ue-ca/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/exceptions.md","content":"# Exceptions\n\n## Overview\n\nException hierarchy for UAC Universal Extensions with proper exit codes and error messages.\n\n## File: src/exceptions.py\n\n```python\nclass ExecutionError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for all extension errors.\"\"\"\n    exit_code: int = 1\n    message: str = \"Execution Failed\"\n\n    def __init__(self, message: Optional[str] = None):\n        if message:\n            self.message = f\"{self.message}: {message}\"\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n```\n\n## Exception Types\n\n### Exit Code 1 - User/Input Errors\n\n**DataValidationError** - Invalid input field\n```python\nraise DataValidationError(\"Port must be 1-65535\")\n```\n\n**UnexpectedSystemError** - Unexpected system error\n```python\nraise UnexpectedSystemError(f\"Unexpected: {str(e)}\")\n```\n\n## Usage Patterns\n\n### Exception Flow\n\n**extension.py** (extension_start) catches 2 base cases:\n1. **ExecutionError** - All custom extension exceptions (proper exit codes, error messages)\n2. **Exception** - Any unexpected errors (system errors, bugs)\n\nAll other code should raise exceptions and let extension_start handle them.\n\n### In Utilities (Convert Third-Party Exceptions)\n\nUtilities convert third-party exceptions to custom ExecutionError subclasses:\n\n```python\nfrom exceptions import ResourceNotFoundError, ServiceConnectionError\n\ndef find_resource(resource_id: str):\n    \"\"\"Find resource by ID.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return api_client.get_resource(resource_id)\n    except ThirdPartyNotFound:  # Third-party exception\n        raise ResourceNotFoundError(f\"Resource {resource_id} not found\")\n\ndef delete_resource_api(resource):\n    \"\"\"Delete resource via API.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return api_client.delete(resource)\n    except ThirdPartyConnectionError:  # Third-party exception\n        raise ServiceConnectionError(\"Cannot connect to API\")\n```\n\n### In Actions (Let Exceptions Propagate)\n\nActions call utilities and let exceptions propagate to extension_start:\n\n```python\ndef delete_resource(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    # NO try-except - let utilities raise custom exceptions\n    resource = find_resource(input_data.resource_id)  # Raises ResourceNotFoundError\n    delete_resource_api(resource)  # Raises ServiceConnectionError\n\n    return ActionOutput(resource_id=resource.id)\n    # extension_start catches ExecutionError and Exception\n```\n\n### In Validation\n\n```python\nfrom exceptions import DataValidationError\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\n\ndef _validate_port(self):\n    if not (1 <= self.port <= 65535):\n        exc = DataValidationError(\"Port must be 1-65535\")\n        extension_manager.add_error(exc, field=\"port\", value=self.port)\n```\n\n### In Actions (Error Collection - ONLY Time to Use try-except)\n\nUse try-except in actions ONLY for strategic error collection (batch processing):\n\n```python\nfrom exceptions import ExecutionError\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\n\ndef batch_process(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    processed = 0\n    failed = []\n\n    # Try-except ONLY to continue processing despite errors\n    for item in items:\n        try:\n            process_item(item)  # Utility raises custom exception\n            processed += 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Collect error and continue to next item\n            extension_manager.add_error(e, item=item.id)\n            failed.append(item.id)\n\n    if failed:\n        # Store partial results before raising\n        extension_manager.set_result({\n            \"processed\": processed,\n            \"failed\": failed,\n            \"total\": len(items)\n        })\n        raise ExecutionError(f\"Failed {len(failed)} of {len(items)} items\")\n\n    return ActionOutput(processed=processed)\n```\n\n**This is the ONLY valid use of try-except in actions** - when you need to collect errors and continue processing.\n\n## Custom Exceptions\n\nAdd custom exception types for your extension:\n\n```python\nclass RateLimitError(ExecutionError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when rate limit is exceeded.\"\"\"\n    exit_code = 2\n    message = \"Rate Limit Exceeded\"\n\nclass InvalidFormatError(ExecutionError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when data format is invalid.\"\"\"\n    exit_code = 1\n    message = \"Invalid Format\"\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```python\nif response.status == 429:\n    raise RateLimitError(f\"Retry after {retry_after}s\")\n\nif not validate_format(data):\n    raise InvalidFormatError(f\"Expected JSON, got {type(data)}\")\n```\n\n## Error Message Format\n\n```python\n# Good - Clear and actionable\nraise DataValidationError(\"Port must be between 1 and 65535\")\nraise ResourceNotFoundError(f\"Resource '{resource_id}' not found in region '{region}'\")\n\n# Bad - Vague or not actionable\nraise ExecutionError(\"Error\")\nraise ExecutionError(\"Something went wrong\")\n```\n\nInclude context in the message to help debug:\n```python\nraise ServiceConnectionError(\n    f\"Failed to connect to {endpoint} after {retries} retries: {str(e)}\"\n)\n```\n","numLines":175,"startLine":1,"totalLines":175}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqGUYQbYymPzFGDu4aQNSK","duration_ms":2}

