2026-09-24 12:27:19 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"be7fe2a4-925e-4d9e-84f7-b622b1f02f43","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-aws-object-storage-demo/be7fe2a4-925e-4d9e-84f7-b622b1f02f43.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/aws-object-storage-demo","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","agent_id":"a9bd597c0c6047262","agent_type":"ue-ca:implementation:action-developer","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/iss-ue-ca-plugin/claude/uac/ue-ca/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/actions.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/iss-ue-ca-plugin/claude/uac/ue-ca/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/actions.md","content":"# Actions\n\n## Overview\n\nActions are the business logic implementations mapped to extension operations. Each action receives `InputFields` and returns `ActionOutput`.\n\n## File: src/actions/__init__.py\n\n```python\nfrom actions.output import ActionOutput\n\n# Import your action functions\nfrom actions.create_resource import create_resource\nfrom actions.delete_resource import delete_resource\n\n# Map action names to functions\nACTION_MAPPER = {\n    \"create\": create_resource,\n    \"delete\": delete_resource\n}\n```\n\n## Action Function Signature\n\n**Action functions ONLY accept `input_data: InputFields`**\n\n```python\nfrom fields import InputFields\nfrom actions import ActionOutput\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nfrom exceptions import ExecutionError\n\n\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\ndef my_action(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    \"\"\"\n    Action implementation.\n\n    **IMPORTANT: Actions ONLY take input_data parameter - OutputFields is created inside the function!**\n\n    Args:\n        input_data: Validated input fields (ONLY parameter!)\n\n    Returns:\n        ActionOutput with results\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check cancellation\n    if extension_manager.is_cancelled():\n        raise OperationCancelledError(\"Cancelled\")\n\n    # Perform operation\n    result = perform_operation(input_data)\n\n    # Return output\n    return ActionOutput(\n        resource_id=result.id,\n        resource_name=result.name,\n        details={\"status\": \"success\"}\n    )\n```\n\n## OutputFields Usage (Real-time UI Updates)\n\n\nUse OutputFields for progress tracking and status updates:\n\n```python\nfrom fields.output import OutputFields\n\ndef process_items_action(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    # 1. Create and initialize OutputFields\n    output_fields = OutputFields(\n        status=\"Starting\",\n        progress=\"0%\",\n        items_processed=0\n    )\n\n    # 2. Access previous run data if needed\n    if input_data.previous_output:\n        last_id = input_data.previous_output.last_processed_id\n        # Resume from last processed...\n\n    # 3. Update UI in real-time during processing\n    #    Each update() call automatically syncs to UAC Controller\n    for i, item in enumerate(items):\n        output_fields.update(\n            status=\"Processing\",\n            progress=f\"{i+1}/{len(items)}\",\n            items_processed=i+1\n        )\n        process(item)\n\n    # 4. Set final state\n    output_fields.update(\n        status=\"Completed\",\n        progress=\"100%\"\n    )\n\n    # 5. Return ActionOutput (OutputFields already synced, don't pass it)\n    return ActionOutput(\n        items_processed=len(items)\n    )\n```\n\n**OutputFields automatically sync to UAC Controller - no need to return them!**\n\n## Error Handling\n\n**Actions should raise errors - extension.py catches them**\n\nAll error catching is handled by extension.py. Actions only use try-except for strategic error collection.\n\n**Fail fast (NO try-except):**\n```python\n# Stop immediately on critical errors - just raise\n# Utilities raise custom exceptions, actions let them propagate\nconnection = connect_to_service()  # Raises ServiceConnectionError if fails\ndata = fetch_data(connection)      # Raises DataFetchError if fails\nresult = process_data(data)        # Raises ProcessingError if fails\n\nreturn ActionOutput(result=result)\n```\n\n**Strategic error collection (YES try-except, to continue processing):**\n```python\n# Use try-except ONLY when you need to collect errors and continue\n# This is for batch processing where you want to process all items despite failures\nfor item in items:\n    try:\n        process(item)  # Utility raises exception\n    except Exception as e:\n        exc = ExecutionError(f\"Failed: {item}\")\n        extension_manager.add_error(exc, item=item)\n        # Continue to next item\n\n# Set partial result before raising\nextension_manager.set_result({\"processed\": 50, \"failed\": 10})\nraise ExecutionError(\"Batch processing completed with errors\")\n```\n\n**Rule: Only use try-except in actions for strategic error collection (continuing despite errors). For all other cases, let errors raise naturally.**\n\n","numLines":143,"startLine":1,"totalLines":143}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KzF1rHEoFMroyCDFM4Gvu8","duration_ms":2}

